<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Neo Analytics - FAQ</title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@500;600;700&display=swap"
    rel="stylesheet"
  />
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/styles.css" />
</head>
<body>
  <main class="container">
    <nav class="navbar" data-animate style="--delay: 0s;">
      <a class="nav-brand" href="/dashboard">
        <span class="nav-mark">N3</span>
        <span class="nav-copy">
          <span class="nav-title">Neo Analytics</span>
          <span class="nav-subtitle">Real usage explorer</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <div class="nav-links">
        <a class="nav-link {{#if nav.dashboard}}is-active{{/if}}" href="/dashboard">Dashboard</a>
        <a class="nav-link {{#if nav.faq}}is-active{{/if}}" href="/faq">FAQ</a>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <header class="hero faq-hero" data-animate style="--delay: 0.04s;">
      <div>
        <span class="pill">FAQ</span>
        <h1>Clear answers to how Neo Analytics works.</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">
          We translate on-chain activity into a simple picture of real usage,
          with transparent rules and daily updates.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-meta">
          <span class="pill">Neo N3 RPC data</span>
          <span class="pill">Daily ingestion</span>
          <span class="pill">Deterministic rules</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-hero-card">
        <div class="faq-stat">
          <span>Classification</span>
          <strong>Swap, transfer, gas claim</strong>
          <p>Order of precedence: swap, gas claim, transfer.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-stat">
          <span>Token labels</span>
          <strong>Symbol first, contract name fallback</strong>
          <p>Unknown contracts keep the hash as a last resort.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="faq-grid" data-animate style="--delay: 0.08s;">
      <article class="faq-card">
        <div class="faq-card-header">
          <span class="faq-tag">Real usage</span>
          <span class="faq-code">NORMAL_TRANSFER</span>
        </div>
        <h3>What counts as real usage?</h3>
        <p>
          Real usage includes swaps and normal transfers, while gas claims and
          self-transfers are excluded. The goal is to focus on activity that
          represents actual user intent.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="faq-card">
        <div class="faq-card-header">
          <span class="faq-tag">Swaps</span>
          <span class="faq-code">SWAP</span>
        </div>
        <h3>How are swaps detected?</h3>
        <p>
          We flag transactions with swap-like methods and multiple transfers.
          Known DEX contracts and swap notifications also count as swaps.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="faq-card">
        <div class="faq-card-header">
          <span class="faq-tag">Claims</span>
          <span class="faq-code">GAS_CLAIM</span>
        </div>
        <h3>Why are GAS claims separated?</h3>
        <p>
          Claims are system distributions with no sender address. They are
          important to track, but they do not reflect user-initiated transfers.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="faq-card">
        <div class="faq-card-header">
          <span class="faq-tag">Coverage</span>
          <span class="faq-code">NEP-17</span>
        </div>
        <h3>Which transfers are counted?</h3>
        <p>
          The pipeline reads NEP-17 transfer notifications. Native NEO and GAS
          are labeled automatically, and other tokens resolve by symbol when possible.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="faq-card">
        <div class="faq-card-header">
          <span class="faq-tag">Support</span>
          <span class="faq-code">COMMUNITY</span>
        </div>
        <h3>Who funds this project?</h3>
        <p>
          This project is not funded by anyone. I cover the server costs and spend my own
          time to keep it running. If you want to support it, Neo/GAS or any N3 token
          donations to <span class="mono">NgdZvkR3bvsXuScWFrTQWfNhALarQ76CEr</span> are appreciated.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-accordion" data-animate style="--delay: 0.12s;">
      <div class="faq-accordion-header">
        <h2>More details</h2>
        <p class="summary-subtitle">Short answers for deeper dives.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-stack">
        <details open>
          <summary>How often is data updated?</summary>
          <p>
            The ingestion job runs daily and retries hourly if a day is missing.
            Admin endpoints can backfill ranges when needed.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I query the raw data?</summary>
          <p>
            Use the API endpoints under <span class="mono">/api/stats</span> for
            totals, asset stats, methods, and contract breakdowns.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What happens to unknown tokens?</summary>
          <p>
            We attempt to fetch the symbol first, then the contract name.
            If those calls fail, the contract hash is displayed.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Why are zero-amount transfers ignored?</summary>
          <p>
            Zero-amount events can be noisy and do not represent user activity.
            Ignoring them keeps the metrics aligned with meaningful movement.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-cta" data-animate style="--delay: 0.16s;">
      <div>
        <span class="range-caption">Ready to explore</span>
        <h2>Open the dashboard for live activity.</h2>
        <p class="summary-subtitle">
          Filter by date range and drill into daily details.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a class="button" href="/dashboard">Open dashboard</a>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
